abstract: >-
  Cell-type-resolved progressive dopaminergic lesions in the FlyWire (female)
  and MaleCNS (male) connectome-constrained leaky integrate-and-fire models,
  a surrogate-and-NPE inverse model from phenotype to lesion, a dopamine-gated
  modulation layer, reinforcer-pathway analysis and predictions for fly
  Parkinson's disease models. Companion code for the preprint "Testing
  connectome-constrained Drosophila brain models with simulation-based
  inference: the limits of dopaminergic neuron loss and predictions for
  Parkinson's disease".
